{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"consensus_safety\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"When several replicas each hold the same instance committed and each applies it to its own copy of the state machine, the effect they apply for the instance's key must be the same, because the applied effect is determined by the committed command vector of that instance.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"One instance held committed at three replicas on the captured snapshot, each applied through Exec.executeCommand with a GET probe reading the instance's key from the replicated store.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"each replica's record for the instance is COMMITTED and its dependencies are already satisfied locally\\\",\\\"the key is the one the committed commands touch\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"the production executeCommands loop, watermark advancement and the recovery timeout\\\",\\\"client-visible replies and their timing\\\",\\\"the history that produced each committed record\\\",\\\"N>3 configurations\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB4-applied-state\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"Execution consumes the committed vector: strongconnect applies the commands of each instance in the strongly connected component and marks them EXECUTED, and state.Command.Execute turns those commands into store effects. Two replicas that hold different committed commands for the same instance therefore apply different effects for the same key, which is the agreement property this claim fixes, independently of how the records came to differ.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Applies on the captured snapshot to any instance held committed at more than one replica, including a recovery that committed a NOOP vector for an instance another replica holds with a real command.\\\",\n  \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the harness applies records directly rather than through the production execution loop, so scheduling and watermarks are not covered\\\"],\n  \\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[\\\"an alternative reading is that execution is out of scope for an obligation about adopting a value, which is exactly why this is recorded as its own claim rather than as part of C1\\\"]}}\nb4={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB4-applied-state\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Exec.executeCommand\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":25,\\\"end_line\\\":42,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Execution entry for one committed instance: it checks the committed status, computes the strongly connected component and applies the component's commands.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The applied effect is produced here: the commands of the committed record are executed against the replica's store, so two different committed commands for one instance produce two different effects.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: with one instance held committed at three replicas - the recoverer's NOOP vector and the peer's PUT vector produced by the recovery already confirmed under claim C1 - does applying each record through the real executor leave the same effect for the instance's key? Prefix: the harness drives the recovery, the accept round and the Commit broadcast, then applies each replica's record with Exec.executeCommand and reads the key with a GET probe. Controls: the same event prints the three values and the command each replica held, so a missing application or a mis-set record is visible.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB4-applied-state\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that drives the recovery path, applies each replica's committed instance through the real executor and compares the applied values for the instance's key.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: Replica values are constructed in-package, per-peer buffers replace the transport, and the recovery and execution are entered directly (startRecoveryForInstance, Exec.executeCommand) instead of through the execution loop; the handlers, executor and state application are unmodified\\\",\\\"prepared history: the already-committed record is installed directly, as in the earlier checks\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"committed_reply\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"peer_committed_reply\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"COMMITTED\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"has_command\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB4-applied-state\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The check observes the effect of applying records the run itself produced for one instance; the key and the probe are fixed by the harness, and no expected value is assumed.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Three replicas, one instance, one key; direct execution.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the production loop, watermarks and the timeout are not exercised\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-applied-state\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-applied-effect\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"applied_state_divergence\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB4-applied-state\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB4-applied-state\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports the value each replica's store holds for the instance's key after applying its own committed record, which is the applied effect the claim is about.\\\",\n    \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Each replica's record was COMMITTED and was applied by the real executor.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"committed_reply.instance\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"committed_reply\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-applied-effect\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"applied_state_divergence\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"applied_match\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After each replica applies the instance it holds committed, the replicas' stores must hold the same effect for the instance's key.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"The harness applies records directly with Exec.executeCommand, so scheduling, watermark advancement and the recovery timeout are outside this check.\\\",\\\"Only one instance and one key are compared.\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":6,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"When one instance is held committed at three replicas with different committed commands for it, does applying each record through the executor leave the same effect for the instance's key, or do the replicas' state machines end up holding different effects for the same instance?\\\",\n \\\"importance\\\":\\\"Execution is where a committed decision becomes observable state, so an instance that is committed with different commands at different replicas produces different effects for the same key: replicas then serve different values and can never reconcile without rewriting applied state. This is the applied form of the agreement concern and is stated as its own obligation because the adopted-vector claim excludes execution.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S20-exec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S4-execute-loop\\\",\\\"S6-conflicts-watermarks\\\"],\n \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"one instance committed at three replicas\\\",\\\"the recoverer's NOOP vector against the peer's PUT vector produced by the recovery confirmed under claim C1\\\",\\\"direct execution of each record\\\"],\n \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"each replica holds the instance COMMITTED (recoverer and third replica NOOP, peer PUT)\\\",\\\"the harness applies each record with Exec.executeCommand and probes the instance's key\\\",\\\"the three applied values are compared\\\"],\n \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A1\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B8-scc-closure\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F2-committed-decision\\\"],\n \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B7-execute-scheduler\\\":\\\"the executor path that selects a committed instance and advances execution\\\",\\\"B6-commit-install\\\":\\\"how each replica came to hold a committed record for the instance\\\"},\n \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"consumption\\\",\\\"priority\\\":3,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: execution consumes the committed vector (strongconnect applies the component's commands and marks them EXECUTED; state.Command.Execute turns them into store effects), so different committed commands for one instance cannot produce the same effect (S20-exec, S23-state-conflict-apply)\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the earlier reviewed checks: the three reviewed artifacts for claim C1 established that the recoverer commits NOOP while the peer keeps PUT for the same instance, which is the input this claim observes (S15-handlePrepareReply, S13-handleCommit)\\\"],\n \\\"unknowns\\\":[\\\"the production execution loop, watermark advancement and the recovery timeout are not exercised by the harness\\\",\\\"only one instance and one key are compared\\\"],\n \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"This is the consumption side of the same decision the reviewed artifacts produced: the committed vector per instance is the A1 decision, and the applied effect is what A5 must derive from it. The claim is stated separately from C1 because C1's accepted scope excludes execution, and the property is observed with the real executor and state application.\\\"}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Fixes the applied-state proposition as its own obligation, which is what the previous review required (scope, revision_needed): the claim now includes applying the instance, and the check reuses the harness that drives the confirmed recovery path, applies each replica's committed record with the real executor and compares the effect for the instance's key. The local construction run showed peer 04 against (void) at the other two replicas, i.e. applied_match false; the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-applied-effect.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_recvbal_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and binding are supplied with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; the claim is the applied-state consequence of the confirmed recovery defect and is deliberately separate from C1, whose scope excludes execution.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"question\\\":q,\\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b4]}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-applied-effect.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-applied.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-applied.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
